  "id": "stellate-cell",
  "term": "stellate cell",
  "definition": "In this historical source, a stellate cell is a star-shaped cell of the brain’s supporting tissue, with branching processes. It is described as helping form fibrous networks and sometimes sending processes that attach to blood-vessel walls.",
